- Poorly controlled A1c despite two or more oral agents or need for insulin initiation/adjustment.
- Significant or progressive kidney disease (CKD stage 3b or worse) that complicates med choices.
- Recurrent hypoglycemia or very labile glucose control.
- Uncertainty about best medication class given CV/renal history (e.g., considering SGLT2i or GLP-1 RA with renal dysfunction).
